WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.740
Point a telescope at a star, and
spread its light out into a spectrum.

2
00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.880
You might expect an unbroken
band, from violet to red.

3
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:13.050
Instead, the band is
crossed by thin, dark lines.

4
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.580
Some wavelengths are simply missing.

5
00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.950
What do those dark gaps
reveal about the star?

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.990
In this mission, you'll
make bright line spectra,

7
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.370
using a discharge tube
full of low-pressure gas.

8
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:30.030
Then you'll turn to starlight itself,
and decode what its dark gaps are telling

9
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:30.920
us.

10
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:36.050
Your mission: work out what the dark
gaps in starlight reveal about the star.
